From: Gleb Pesin <dormancygrace@gmail.com>
Subject: [PATCH] vpss, venc: no errors for polls that find no frame

libkvm polls for frames with short timeouts. At high pixel rates it
pre-submits the next frame with a 5 ms wait, and VENC is polled
non-blocking. A poll that finds no frame yet is normal.

Each such poll was still logged as an error, three ways:
- vpss "get chn frame fail, s32MilliSec=5";
- base "jobs wait(0) work(1) done(0)";
- the encoder's "encoder timeout happened in non_block mode".

The stand logged 119 encoder timeouts and 33 VPSS failures since boot.
Its kernel log, archived to the SD card, was mostly these lines.

Only a wait of 100 ms or more that ends without a frame is now an error.
The encoder poll message is a trace. The "Grp invalid," warning for a job
of a group that was just stopped is now debug.
---
--- a/interdrv/base/base_context.c
+++ b/interdrv/base/base_context.c
@@ -264,6 +264,8 @@
 			vb_release_block(s->blk);
 		TAILQ_REMOVE(&jobs->snap_jobs, s, tailq);
 		mutex_unlock(&jobs->dlock);
+		/* A short poll that finds no frame is not an error. */
+		if (timeout_ms < 0 || timeout_ms >= 100)
 		CVI_TRACE_BASE_RATELIMITED(CVI_BASE_DBG_ERR, "Mod(%s) Grp(%d) Chn(%d), jobs wait(%d) work(%d) done(%d)\n"
 			, sys_get_modname(chn.enModId), chn.s32DevId, chn.s32ChnId
 			, FIFO_SIZE(&jobs->waitq), FIFO_SIZE(&jobs->workq), FIFO_SIZE(&jobs->doneq));
--- a/interdrv/vpss/common/vpss.c
+++ b/interdrv/vpss/common/vpss.c
@@ -3056,7 +3056,8 @@
 		return;
 	}
 	if (!vpssCtx[workingGrp] || !vpssCtx[workingGrp]->isStarted) {
-		CVI_TRACE_VPSS(CVI_DBG_WARN, "Grp(%d) invalid,\n", workingGrp);
+		/* A job of a group that was just stopped; nothing to do. */
+		CVI_TRACE_VPSS(CVI_DBG_DEBUG, "Grp(%d) invalid,\n", workingGrp);
 		ctx->workingGrp = VPSS_MAX_GRP_NUM;
 		ctx->workingMask = 0;
 		atomic_set(&ctx->events, 0);
@@ -4590,7 +4591,9 @@
 	memset(pstFrameInfo, 0, sizeof(*pstFrameInfo));
 	ret = base_get_chn_buffer(chn, &blk, s32MilliSec);
 	if (ret != 0 || blk == VB_INVALID_HANDLE) {
-		if (s32MilliSec != 0)
+		/* Only a wait of 100 ms or more that ends without a frame is an
+		 * error; shorter waits poll for a frame that may not be due. */
+		if (s32MilliSec < 0 || s32MilliSec >= 100)
 			CVI_TRACE_VPSS(CVI_DBG_ERR, "Grp(%d) Chn(%d) get chn frame fail, s32MilliSec=%d, ret=%d\n",
 					VpssGrp, VpssChn, s32MilliSec, ret);
 		return CVI_ERR_VPSS_BUF_EMPTY;
--- a/interdrv/cvi_vc_drv/vcodec/sample/main_enc_cvitest.c
+++ b/interdrv/cvi_vc_drv/vcodec/sample/main_enc_cvitest.c
@@ -2500,8 +2500,9 @@
 
 		if (int_reason == -1) {
 			if (s32MilliSec >= 0) {
-				CVI_VC_ERR(
-					"Error : encoder timeout happened in non_block mode\n");
+				/* A poll: the caller retries. */
+				CVI_VC_TRACE(
+					"encoder timeout happened in non_block mode\n");
 				return TE_STA_ENC_TIMEOUT;
 			}
 
